From: Marcin Bober <mbober1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:53:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: honor caller GFP flags for RX buffer allocation

RX buffers were always allocated with GFP_ATOMIC, which fails when the free
lists are empty even though reclaimable memory exists.  The open path passes
GFP_KERNEL, so use the caller flags to allow reclaim during ring setup.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Marcin Bober <mbober1@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -1657,7 +1657,7 @@
 {
 	struct stmmac_rx_queue *rx_q = &dma_conf->rx_queue[queue];
 	struct stmmac_rx_buffer *buf = &rx_q->buf_pool[i];
-	gfp_t gfp = (GFP_ATOMIC | __GFP_NOWARN);
+	gfp_t gfp = flags | __GFP_NOWARN;
 
 	if (priv->dma_cap.host_dma_width <= 32)
 		gfp |= GFP_DMA32;
